From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000004 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: evaluating-cli <noreply@github.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 18:24:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] simx86: publish validator step flags atomically

Publish step_flags with release ordering so the external controller has a
synchronization point for asynchronous lifecycle events that do not
necessarily change the req/ack counters.

Normal node publication still release-stores ack after publishing state. The
additional release store on step_flags is specifically useful for END_ACK and
TARGET_EXIT: a Rust controller can acquire-load step_flags and observe the
preceding CPU/metadata publication without relying on timing or on ack changing
value.

Base: patch 3 on dosemu2/dosemu2@604ce0cdd1a71f657e2a2df623d216d5ab289313
---
diff --git a/src/base/emu-i386/simx86/diis-validator.c b/src/base/emu-i386/simx86/diis-validator.c
--- a/src/base/emu-i386/simx86/diis-validator.c
+++ b/src/base/emu-i386/simx86/diis-validator.c
@@ -300,3 +300,3 @@ static void publish_cpu(unsigned int pc, uint32_t decoded, uint32_t flags)
 	g_shm->runtime_psp = g_runtime_psp;
 	g_shm->decoded_instructions = decoded;
-	g_shm->step_flags = flags;
+	__atomic_store_n(&g_shm->step_flags, flags, __ATOMIC_RELEASE);
@@ -276,4 +276,4 @@ static void mark_target_finished(void)
 		return;
 	g_shm->runtime_psp = 0;
 	g_shm->decoded_instructions = 0;
-	g_shm->step_flags = DIIS_STEP_TARGET_EXIT;
+	__atomic_store_n(&g_shm->step_flags, DIIS_STEP_TARGET_EXIT, __ATOMIC_RELEASE);
